# Generated files that every lane branch changes in the same place conflict textually on every merge into a batch queue
# (backlog row 400). Each gets a merge driver that merges what the file MEANS, registered per clone by
# scripts/setup-merge-drivers.sh (the SessionStart hook runs it; worktrees share the repo config):
#   dev-docs/backlog.md, dev-docs/backlog-done.md   the indexes scripts/backlog-index.sh generates: a 3-way merge by row id
#   playwright/durations.json                       the per-spec seconds table: a 3-way merge by entry, totals recomputed
#   primitives/src/kernel/*                         the decision kernel's committed wasm, its base64 and manifest (row 509): the
#                                                   merged sources are rebuilt (scripts/merge-driver-kernel.py), never merged as bytes
# A clone without the registration falls back to git's text merge (and the old conflicts); scripts/check-merge-drivers.sh
# keeps this file, the driver scripts and the registration command in step.
dev-docs/backlog.md merge=backlog-index
dev-docs/backlog-done.md merge=backlog-index
playwright/durations.json merge=durations
primitives/src/kernel/* merge=kernel-artefact
